      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2.1 Ancient Period"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Ancient period covers major ruling lines including the Satavahana Dynasty (230 BCE – 220 CE), Ikshvaku Dynasty (225–340 CE), and Pallava Dynasty (275–897 CE).",
        "The Medieval period spans dominant empires such as Eastern Chalukyas of Vengi, Rashtrakutas, Western Chalukyas, Kakatiyas, Reddy Kingdoms, Vijayanagara Empire, and Qutb Shahi Dynasty.",
        "The Modern period includes the reign of the Nizam of Hyderabad (1724–1948) and British rule across Andhra.",
        "Key state-building milestones include the original formation of Andhra State and Andhra Pradesh, followed by the bifurcation and formation of Telangana in 2014."
      ],
      "id": "5yai49q"
    },
